 "segments": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "s": 0.35,
   "e": 11.616,
   "text": "To understand our architectural predicament, let us turn our attention to the only definitive proof of general intelligence in the known universe:",
   "dur": 11.266,
   "voiced": 590,
   "sim": 0.848,
   "f0": 128.886,
   "st": 0.119,
   "range_st": 7.511,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "s": 11.892,
   "e": 13.504,
   "text": "the biological brain.",
   "dur": 1.612,
   "voiced": 105,
   "sim": 0.709,
   "f0": 114.428,
   "st": -1.94,
   "range_st": 5.317,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "s": 14.204,
   "e": 21.792,
   "text": "A human brain operates on an astonishingly modest power budget of approximately twenty watts.",
   "dur": 7.588,
   "voiced": 429,
   "sim": 0.83,
   "f0": 140.577,
   "st": 1.623,
   "range_st": 8.392,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "s": 22.873,
   "e": 29.423,
   "text": "That is roughly the energy consumed by a dim refrigerator light bulb.",
   "dur": 6.551,
   "voiced": 369,
   "sim": 0.735,
   "f0": 137.694,
   "st": 1.264,
   "range_st": 7.462,
   "asr": 0.96,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "s": 30.444,
   "e": 38.859,
   "text": "Yet within that microscopic energy footprint, the brain coordinates eighty-six billion living neurons",
   "dur": 8.415,
   "voiced": 517,
   "sim": 0.911,
   "f0": 130.957,
   "st": 0.395,
   "range_st": 7.402,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "s": 38.998,
   "e": 45.469,
   "text": "and over one hundred trillion synaptic junctions with breathtaking cognitive efficiency.",
   "dur": 6.471,
   "voiced": 375,
   "sim": 0.869,
   "f0": 124.704,
   "st": -0.452,
   "range_st": 6.467,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "s": 46.804,
   "e": 51.471,
   "text": "Crucially, the biological brain is never static.",
   "dur": 4.667,
   "voiced": 247,
   "sim": 0.828,
   "f0": 123.374,
   "st": -0.637,
   "range_st": 8.933,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "s": 52.318,
   "e": 55.592,
   "text": "It is in perpetual topological motion.",
   "dur": 3.274,
   "voiced": 189,
   "sim": 0.78,
   "f0": 141.935,
   "st": 1.789,
   "range_st": 6.951,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "s": 55.812,
   "e": 62.403,
   "text": "Through continuous neurogenesis, dendritic arborization, and synaptic spine pruning,",
   "dur": 6.591,
   "voiced": 375,
   "sim": 0.839,
   "f0": 128.591,
   "st": 0.08,
   "range_st": 8.326,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "s": 62.874,
   "e": 69.446,
   "text": "neural circuits physically restructure themselves in real time based on sensory experience.",
   "dur": 6.572,
   "voiced": 359,
   "sim": 0.84,
   "f0": 134.473,
   "st": 0.854,
   "range_st": 9.169,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "s": 70.304,
   "e": 74.738,
   "text": "Under the governing laws of spike-timing-dependent plasticity,",
   "dur": 4.435,
   "voiced": 264,
   "sim": 0.867,
   "f0": 131.997,
   "st": 0.532,
   "range_st": 6.244,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "s": 74.893,
   "e": 79.167,
   "text": "if two neurons repeatedly fire in temporal synchrony,",
   "dur": 4.274,
   "voiced": 265,
   "sim": 0.863,
   "f0": 130.208,
   "st": 0.296,
   "range_st": 10.905,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0,
   "weak": true
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "s": 79.552,
   "e": 90.9,
   "text": "the biochemical junction between them physically thickens, synthesizing new AMPA and NMDA receptors to reinforce the connection.",
   "dur": 11.349,
   "voiced": 608,
   "sim": 0.914,
   "f0": 126.643,
   "st": -0.184,
   "range_st": 6.97,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "s": 91.732,
   "e": 95.234,
   "text": "Conversely, if a pathway remains inactive,",
   "dur": 3.501,
   "voiced": 188,
   "sim": 0.85,
   "f0": 114.442,
   "st": -1.938,
   "range_st": 6.013,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "s": 95.352,
   "e": 104.493,
   "text": "microglia and astrocytic processes prune the unused synapses to conserve precious metabolic energy.",
   "dur": 9.141,
   "voiced": 502,
   "sim": 0.871,
   "f0": 134.255,
   "st": 0.826,
   "range_st": 9.043,
   "asr": 0.963,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "s": 105.353,
   "e": 109.705,
   "text": "The living brain does not separate training from inference.",
   "dur": 4.353,
   "voiced": 263,
   "sim": 0.847,
   "f0": 128.358,
   "st": 0.048,
   "range_st": 8.531,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 5,
   "level": 2
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "s": 110.011,
   "e": 114.515,
   "text": "Every single percept you process, every sentence you read,",
   "dur": 4.504,
   "voiced": 222,
   "sim": 0.85,
   "f0": 129.67,
   "st": 0.224,
   "range_st": 9.929,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "s": 114.769,
   "e": 117.04,
   "text": "and every thought you formulate",
   "dur": 2.27,
   "voiced": 139,
   "sim": 0.805,
   "f0": 119.296,
   "st": -1.219,
   "range_st": 7.496,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "s": 117.208,
   "e": 121.053,
   "text": "physically alters the wiring of your cerebral cortex.",
   "dur": 3.845,
   "voiced": 230,
   "sim": 0.787,
   "f0": 124.844,
   "st": -0.432,
   "range_st": 7.666,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "s": 122.105,
   "e": 127.091,
   "text": "Biological computation is event-driven and asynchronous.",
   "dur": 4.986,
   "voiced": 275,
   "sim": 0.885,
   "f0": 125.723,
   "st": -0.311,
   "range_st": 8.387,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "s": 127.613,
   "e": 135.92,
   "text": "Neurons communicate via sparse millisecond electrical action potentials at frequencies of only one to ten hertz,",
   "dur": 8.307,
   "voiced": 468,
   "sim": 0.859,
   "f0": 128.895,
   "st": 0.121,
   "range_st": 9.375,
   "asr": 0.938,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 21,
   "s": 136.175,
   "e": 140.322,
   "text": "avoiding wasteful continuous synchronization clocks.",
   "dur": 4.148,
   "voiced": 237,
   "sim": 0.863,
   "f0": 138.978,
   "st": 1.425,
   "range_st": 8.608,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 22,
   "s": 141.311,
   "e": 149.737,
   "text": "Now compare this living, breathing architecture to a modern artificial intelligence data center.",
   "dur": 8.426,
   "voiced": 479,
   "sim": 0.871,
   "f0": 119.305,
   "st": -1.218,
   "range_st": 4.75,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 23,
   "s": 150.437,
   "e": 160.846,
   "text": "A frontier GPU cluster consumes megawatts of electrical power, requiring massive liquid cooling towers and industrial substations.",
   "dur": 10.409,
   "voiced": 588,
   "sim": 0.877,
   "f0": 130.408,
   "st": 0.323,
   "range_st": 8.403,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 24,
   "s": 161.329,
   "e": 170.708,
   "text": "Inside, millions of identical matrix operations are broadcast across rigid, invariant systolic arrays.",
   "dur": 9.379,
   "voiced": 546,
   "sim": 0.823,
   "f0": 117.735,
   "st": -1.447,
   "range_st": 5.831,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 25,
   "s": 171.482,
   "e": 176.674,
   "text": "Why couldn't our artificial neural networks work like living biology?",
   "dur": 5.192,
   "voiced": 333,
   "sim": 0.807,
   "f0": 123.364,
   "st": -0.639,
   "range_st": 7.5,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 26,
   "s": 176.894,
   "e": 188.639,
   "text": "Why did computer science abandon the living dream of continuous, self-organizing plasticity in favor of frozen tensors?",
   "dur": 11.745,
   "voiced": 653,
   "sim": 0.884,
   "f0": 122.924,
   "st": -0.7,
   "range_st": 4.242,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  }
 ]
